# SEO (Non-Negotiable — Priority 1)

Personal site goal: **discoverability for recruiters** and **technical credibility** via blog.

**Owner priority:** SEO is as important as initial load speed — static HTML, complete metadata, and crawlable content beat interactive flourishes.

## Rendering Strategy

| Page | Strategy |
|------|----------|
| Home, About, Skills, Projects, Experience, Contact | **SSG** — static at build |
| Blog index | **SSG** with `generateStaticParams` |
| Blog post | **SSG** from MDX |
| Contact form submit | API route or Nest — **noindex** on API responses |

```tsx
export const dynamic = 'force-static'; // default for marketing pages
```

## Metadata (every public page)

Use `generateMetadata` with locale-aware titles.

```tsx
export async function generateMetadata({ params }): Promise<Metadata> {
  const t = await getTranslations({ locale: params.locale, namespace: 'metadata.home' });
  const base = process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL ?? 'http://localhost:3000';
  return {
    title: t('title'),
    description: t('description'),
    openGraph: {
      title: t('title'),
      description: t('description'),
      url: `${base}/${params.locale}`,
      type: 'website',
      locale: params.locale === 'fa' ? 'fa_IR' : 'en_US',
      images: [{ url: `${base}/og-image.png`, width: 1200, height: 630 }],
    },
    alternates: {
      canonical: `${base}/${params.locale}`,
      languages: {
        en: `${base}/en`,
        fa: `${base}/fa`,
        'x-default': `${base}/en`,
      },
    },
  };
}
```

## URL Structure

- Clean paths: `/en/projects`, `/fa/blog/my-post`, `/en/contact`
- No query-string-only pages for primary content
- Blog slugs: kebab-case, English slug even for FA posts (or matching slug pair via `translationSlug`)

## Required Root Files

- `frontend/app/sitemap.ts` — all locales and blog posts
- `frontend/app/robots.ts` — allow public pages; disallow `/api/` if any

## Structured Data (JSON-LD)

Inject in Server Components via `<script type="application/ld+json">`.

| Page | Schema |
|------|--------|
| Home / About | `Person` + `ProfilePage` |
| Blog post | `BlogPosting` + `BreadcrumbList` |
| Site-wide | `WebSite` with `inLanguage: ['en', 'fa']` |

```json
{
  "@type": "Person",
  "name": "Hossein Khalili",
  "jobTitle": "Front-End Developer",
  "url": "{{NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL}}",
  "sameAs": ["https://linkedin.com/in/...", "https://t.me/..."],
  "knowsAbout": ["React", "Next.js", "TypeScript", "WebSocket"]
}
```

## Blog SEO

- Unique `<h1>` = post title
- Meta description from frontmatter `description` (≤ 160 chars)
- `article:published_time`, `article:modified_time` in Open Graph
- Internal links to related projects/posts where natural

## Indexing Rules

- `robots: { index: true }` — all public marketing and blog pages
- `noindex` — thank-you page after form if thin duplicate; API routes
- Resume PDF: link with descriptive anchor text; optional `noindex` on raw PDF path

## Content Quality

- One `<h1>` per page
- Heading hierarchy: `h1 → h2 → h3` without skips
- Image `alt` text descriptive in page language
- External project links: `rel="noopener noreferrer"`; do not claim ownership of domains you don't control in schema

## Performance ↔ SEO (same priority)

Google ranks on experience signals — treat SEO and speed as one requirement:

- **Hero LCP:** typography-first or CSS-only hero preferred; no large above-fold image unless `priority` + optimized + ≤ 100 KB target
- **Critical content in initial HTML** — name, title, summary, nav links must render without waiting for client JS hydration
- **No client-only rendering** for indexable pages — marketing routes are Server Components + SSG
- **Font loading** must not block text visibility — `display: swap`, subset per locale
- **hreflang + canonical** on every indexable page — broken i18n SEO is a ship blocker
- See `performance.mdc` for numeric budgets and Lighthouse gates

## Ship Gates (SEO)

Before merge/deploy, verify on **`/en` and `/fa`**:

- [ ] Unique `title` + `description` + canonical on every public page
- [ ] `sitemap.xml` and `robots.txt` include all locales and blog posts
- [ ] JSON-LD validates (Rich Results Test)
- [ ] One `<h1>` per page; logical heading order
- [ ] View Page Source shows main text content (not empty shell waiting for JS)
